# Transitive advisories that cannot be remediated here and cannot reach users.
#
# This package publishes `dist/` only and declares zero runtime dependencies, so
# nothing below is present in the npm tarball. Both arrive through the n8n
# development toolchain: nanoid via @n8n/utils, which pins 3.3.8 exactly, and
# uuid via @langchain/* which requires ^10, while the fix is 11.1.1 — outside
# the range. Neither can be bumped without the upstream package changing.
#
# Revisit when n8n updates its dependencies.

# nanoid: custom generators can loop indefinitely when size is zero
CVE-2026-67213
# nanoid: non-secure generators can loop indefinitely with negative size
CVE-2026-67214
# nanoid: predictable ID generation from an integer overflow in the size argument
CVE-2026-73086
# uuid: missing buffer bounds check in v3/v5/v6 when buf is provided
CVE-2026-41907
